David is here.
>
You are carrying a leather briefcase and the list.
You are wearing an old school tie, a jacket, a shirt, some trousers and a watch.
"I've got to go now," says David. "My office is on the floor below if you have any problems. You have to walk through my secretary's office to get there. Bye."
David goes into Margaret's office.
>
The leather briefcase is now open.
>
There are no major surprises in the list of early bookings. The shares are all safe, steady earners. The sort of shares pension funds and unit trust companies love.
>
The desk is covered with tea and coffee stains.
>
Margaret's Office
Margaret has made a great effort to make this room homely by having flowers next to the typewriter on her desk, putting pictures of her family on the wall and keeping the place clean and tidy. However, it will remain an unsightly place due to her presence. The corridor for the second floor is beyond an exit to the east.
Margaret is sitting at her desk, typing away.
"Hello Mr. Rogers," she says. "I hope you like your new office. If you need anything I'll be here, but you'll just want to settle in today I expect."
>
I don't understand talk
>
Corridor
The faint sound of car horns comes from behind a fire door to the south in this gloomy corridor. Further up the corridor to the north is the dealing room and William Hughes's office. Margaret's office is to the west, opposite the building's gurgling bathroom.
>
You open the fire door first.
Fire Escape
As the lift constantly breaks down, this fire escape is used in preference more often than not. A fire door to the north leads to the second floor, where you have your office.
